# Chapter 5, part 7: the Print Error marker, which only the Editor makes.
# Chapter 6 holds the Error Log and the way the markers are made
# (print-errors); chapter 3 holds Find Next Error (edit-c-find-error).

.h2 Print Error [markers-errors]
.ix Print Error marker
.ix Marker, Print Error
.ix PRINT ERROR
.ix Errors in the text
A Print Error marker is a note that the Editor leaves in the text at the
place where Print or Preview found something wrong: in front of an equation
that is not TeX math, in front of a picture whose file is not there, in front
of a character that no font has.  It carries the message of the Printer and
its code, so that the error and its place stay in the document until they are
fixed and nothing has to be written down.  {b:Only the Editor makes it.}
No panel, key, command, macro or library entry inserts one, and it is not in
the Marker Commands list.  The user may only find it
({n:edit-c-find-error}), read it and delete it.
.table 12 48
Item | Value
Panel | None: a read-only box with the text (below).
Made by | A Print (Draft or Final) or a Preview of the Editor, after the
 Printer has typeset the part ({n:print-errmarks}).
Not made by | The print and preview modes of the Editor: they have no
 document open and show the faults as text.
Global setting | None.  It is not changed by Global, Marker.
.end
.h3 What the marker holds
The marker holds three plain texts.  They are not fields of a panel: the
Editor writes them and they cannot be changed.
.table 7 34 16
Part | Holds | Example
Message | The message, in plain English.  When the place was only guessed, it
 | ends with "(The exact place was not found; this is the nearest.)". | Picture
 | file not found: {c:pics/missing.png} (looked in /work/memo).
Code | The kind of the error, as in {x:print-errkinds}. | picture-missing
Run | The run that found it: P for a Print, V for a Preview.  A new run
 | replaces only the markers of its own kind. | P
.end

.h3 On the screen
In every display mode, the label is
.code
[PRINT ERROR: MESSAGE [code]]
.end
for example "[PRINT ERROR: Picture file not found: {c:pics/missing.png}
(looked in /work/memo). [picture-missing]]".  It is drawn in the color of
the markers, in bold and underlined, so that it cannot be taken for text.
The Hidden mode of Global, Marker does not hide it, and the Display Hidden
Markers setting does not change it.  A label is as wide as its text: a long one
continues on the next row, and the last row is cut at the right edge of the
window.  The whole
text is in the message line when {k:Ctrl-F8} lands on the marker (the
message line is cut at the width of the window too) and in the box of
{k:Alt-F12}, which wraps it.  The marker is one item of the text, as
other markers are: the cursor stops on it.
.pic pictures/markers-errors.png 5 The text of the test document after Print: Print Error markers in bold and underlined, the cursor on the second.

.h3 The read-only box
{k:Alt-F12} or {k:Ctrl-F12} with the cursor on the marker, which is what
opens the panel of any other marker, opens a box titled
"Print Error (read only; Del removes it)" that holds the message with the
code in brackets, and "Press any key".  Any key closes it.  Nothing in it can
be changed, and the marker is not changed.  On any other place the keys open
the Marker Commands list, which does not list the Print Error.
.pic pictures/markers-errors-box.png 5 The read-only box of a Print Error marker, opened with Alt-F12.

.h3 When printed
Never.  A document with Print Error markers gives the same pages as one
without them; the
text export, Screen Image and the printout of the text leave it out as well.
A Print Error marker does not take a place on the page, does not break a
line and does not change the page count.  What is printed is the Error Log
({n:print-errlog}) and, when the print failed, the banner and the small labels
E1, W2 ... that the Printer puts at the same places in the pages
({n:print-failed}).  A label has the number of the entry of the Error Log.

.h3 Delete, copy, cut and paste
.table 20 40
Action | What happens
{k:Del} on the marker | Removes it, like one character.
{k:Backspace} just after it | Removes it.
Remove (Print, Errors) | Removes the marker under the cursor, or shows "The
 cursor is not on a Print Error".
Remove All (Print, Errors) | Removes every Print Error marker of the
 document and shows how many.
Copy, Cut | The marker is not put on the clipboard.  Cut takes it out of the
 text with the rest of the cut text, but it is not in what is pasted.  A block
 that is copied has none in it.
Paste | A Print Error marker that is in the clipboard is dropped.
Print, Preview again | Takes out the old markers of its own kind in the part
 that was printed, and puts the new ones in ({n:print-errmarks}).
.end

.h3 Saving and loading
Save writes the markers into the document with the rest of the text, and they
load again with their text.  The Editor marks the document as changed when
markers are put in (the star before the name in the status line).  A print
never writes the document: the file on disk is as it was until Save.  Remove
Print Errors before saving if the markers are not wanted in the file.

.h3 Edges
- A document with Print Error markers prints as one without: the markers never
  change the pages, and the Error Log never lists the markers themselves.
  The labels of a failed print are made again by each print, from what that
  print found.
- A marker that stands where the document was changed after the run still
  shows its text of the time of the run.  Print again to renew them.
- A Preview of a block or of a section marks only the blocks of that part.
- Several faults at one place are in the order in which the Printer found
  them.
